  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>caspofungin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J02AX04</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Abdul-Aziz MH et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>critically ill patients receiving ECMO</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>caspofungin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_caspofungin/Caspofungin_AbdulAziz2025_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL (L/h)</td><td>0.55</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V (L)</td><td>8.13</td><td>L</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr></table><h4>About caspofungin</h4><p>Caspofungin is an antifungal used to treat candidiasis and aspergillosis. It is an approved, systemically used antifungal and is authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420875\">Wikidata Q420875</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Caspofungin\">Caspofungin</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Abdul-Aziz MH et al. (2025). Population pharmacokinetics of caspofungin in critically ill patients receiving extracorporeal membrane oxygenation-an ASAP ECMO study. <i>Antimicrobial agents and chemotherapy 69(2):e0143524</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1128/aac.01435-24\">10.1128/aac.01435-24</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39692515\">39692515</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Abdul-Aziz_2025: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
